\section*{Margulis–Platonov normal subgroups over global function fields}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 018; 2026-10-05), the asserted result is that every noncentral abstract normal subgroup of rational points of an absolutely almost simple simply connected group over a global function field is determined by open normal data at anisotropic places, including characteristic two.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
Let $k$ be a global function field and $G/k$ absolutely almost simple simply connected. Put $A(G)=\{v:\operatorname{rank}_{k_v}G=0\}$, a finite set, $H_A=\prod_{v\in A(G)}G(k_v)$ with product topology, and let $\delta_A:G(k)\to H_A$ be diagonal. For every abstract normal subgroup $N$ not contained in the center, the claim is
\[
 \exists W\triangleleft H_A\text{ open}:\quad N=\delta_A^{-1}(W).
\]
All positive characteristics are included, also when $G$ is globally anisotropic. Abstract normality does not presume topological closure.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 018; 2026-10-05), products of torus powers provide approximation in prescribed cosets. Finite additive Fourier analysis replaces integer-dilation recurrence, with a characteristic-two power-subfield calculation; finite simple-group obstructions and local character control complete the normal-subgroup argument.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 018; 2026-10-05).

